  "title": "somatomotor",
  "description": "A multi-modal neuroimaging dataset combining structural MRI (T1w), magnetoencephalography (MEG), and EEG recorded during electrical median nerve stimulation at the right wrist. Participants responded to each stimulus by lifting the left index finger as quickly as possible, allowing study of somatosensory and motor responses. Anatomical fiducials were digitized to align MEG with MRI, and event triggers mark stimuli and finger-lift responses.",
  "methods_description": "MEG and EEG were recorded during right median nerve electrical stimulation with left index finger lift responses. Three anatomical fiducials (nasion, left and right pre-auricular points) were digitized for MEG-MRI alignment. Triggers 32 (somatosensory stimulus) and 16 (finger lift response) are stored in the .fif files and events .tsv files.",
